draft_notes.limitations:
The palette edge is fixed by d4 rather than inferred from the pixels. This is valid because the D4 transform applies uniformly to the whole episode.

The program assumes the generator's domain:
- exactly one line, perpendicular to the palette edge;
- the line never touches the palette edge (r0 >= 2 holds because m >= 4 and boost <= 2);
- the line runs to the far edge;
- the background is palette[5].

The palette cell above the line is always background, and the line cells are left unchanged, matching the generator.

No constructor defects or fixture contradictions were found. All fixtures match the r0+|x-c| staircase. I have not run any tests.
